# The Ring's level 1 (Player.setRingLevel): "Your Ring-bearer can't be
# blocked by creatures with greater power" -- Mode$ CantBlockBy with
# ValidBlockerRelative$ Creature.powerGTX, X = Count$CardPower, the
# attacker's power. The Ring-bearer Grizzly Bears (2/2) attacks; the AI
# blocks with its own Grizzly Bears (2/2), the equal-power creature CanBlock
# accepts. Hill Giant (3/3) stays home: declaring it as a blocker would be
# an illegal declaration (CR 509.1b, ADR-0024), an error rather than a
# dropped pairing. Each Bears takes 2 damage, the Hill Giant none.
startturn human
advance 5
queue attackers 1
declareattackers
advance
queue blocks 3=1
declareblockers
advance
advance
combatdamage
